# Lexical lookup reads through enclosing scopes

Verifies name resolution walks parent scopes recursively: the innermost block
reads `x` from the root scope and `y` from its immediate parent. The final read
after both blocks proves the root binding is still visible there.

>>> source
let x: int = 10

{
    let y: int = 20

    {
        print(x)
        print(y)
    }
}

print(x)

<<< stdout
10
20
10

<<< stderr
